  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-3 After Battle Cutscene 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Somehow, I don't know how, I won against him. He hit the chairs near
      him and fell to the ground. I let him go, making him lose his confidence. Maybe
      because of my small size, my classmate thought that I was smart at fighting.
      A boy challenged me and I accepted but lost, almost breaking my head.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I don't want to take up time telling how many beatings I got, nor try
      to tell how much it hurt. I used to win in competitions, as no one was better
      than me. When I went out with my companions, they teased me with nicknames.
      But every friend that I have were very kind to me that I didn't too much about
      their teasing. Later, some of them were my schoolmates in Manila and came my
      turn to tease.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Near the house of my schoolmaster lived his father-in-law, generally
      called Juancho. Juancho let me help him with his paintings, and in turn I learned
      how to paint from him. I had liked this style of art that our classmates called
      Jose Guevarra, another pupil, and myself the class painters.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
